# What VeriFlow will not index in this repository.
#
# gitignore syntax: a bare name matches at any depth, a trailing slash means a directory, a leading
# slash anchors to the root, `*` stays inside a segment, `**` crosses segments, and `!` re-includes.
# node_modules, build output and dot-directories are excluded already and need no rule here.
#
# This is not the same list as .gitignore. These files are committed and belong in the repository —
# they are simply not the application, and indexing them puts mockup routes in the call graph and
# mockup folders in the module registry.

# The F001–F006 design mockups: a Next.js app whose only purpose was to draw the screens. Its two
# route handlers were the only entry points VeriFlow detected in this repository, which made the call
# graph six functions of example code and nothing of the product.
/artifacts/

# Fixtures and dumps read as data by the tests, not as code that runs.
/tests/fixtures/
